N-th roots (round 19, decision U19.3): Ctrl+5 (Ctrl+%) makes a root with an index, or moves between a root's
index and radicand (giving a square root an index). The canonical text is `((surd(x, n)))`, the real n-th root.

=== Ctrl+5 makes an n-th root with the caret in its index; Ctrl+5 again goes to the radicand
--- before
#% cell
y = ▮
--- keys
Ctrl+5 "3" Ctrl+5 "x+1"
--- after
#% cell typeset
y = ((surd(x+1▮, 3)))
--- boxes
y = √[3](x+1▮)

=== Ctrl+% is Ctrl+5
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Ctrl+% "4" Ctrl+% "z"
--- boxes
√[4](z▮)

=== Ctrl+5 in a square root gives it an index
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Ctrl+2 "x" Ctrl+5 "3"
--- boxes
√[3▮](x)

=== Ctrl+5 in the index goes back to the end of the radicand
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Ctrl+2 "x" Ctrl+5 "3" Ctrl+5 "y"
--- boxes
√[3](xy▮)

=== Backspace at the start of the radicand steps to the index's end, deleting nothing
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Ctrl+5 "3" Ctrl+5 "x" Left Backspace
--- boxes
√[3▮](x)

=== Backspace in an emptied index leaves a square root
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Ctrl+5 "3" Ctrl+5 "x" Left Backspace Backspace Backspace
--- boxes
√(▮x)

=== Delete at the end of a filled root's radicand writes it as linear text, the term kept
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Ctrl+5 "3" Ctrl+5 "x" Delete
--- after
#% cell
surd(x, 3)▮

=== a typed operator after the root stays outside it
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Ctrl+5 "3" Ctrl+5 "x" Ctrl+Space "+1"
--- after
#% cell typeset
((surd(x, 3)))+1▮

=== undo of the root is one step; redo brings it back
--- before
#% cell
a+▮
--- keys
Ctrl+5 Ctrl+Z
--- after
#% cell
a+▮

=== an n-th root copied from one cell pastes as an n-th root into another
--- before
#% cell typeset
((surd(x, 3)))▮

#% cell
y+
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+C Click(1,2) Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell typeset
((surd(x, 3)))

#% cell typeset
y+((surd(x, 3)))▮
--- clip
text "surd(x, 3)"
boxes "((surd(x, 3)))"

=== evaluating a cell with an n-th root sends the real root
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Ctrl+5 "3" Ctrl+5 "8" Shift+Enter
--- after
#% cell label=1 typeset
((surd(8, 3)))
#% output n=1
#= ((surd(8, 3)))
‖

=== Paste as math reads another program's text as boxes: the copied cell comes back identical
--- before
#% cell typeset
y = ((1)/(x)) + ((surd(x, 3))) + ((e)^(((sqrt(t)))))▮

#% cell
z
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+Shift+C Click(1,1) Ctrl+Shift+V
--- after
#% cell typeset
y = ((1)/(x)) + ((surd(x, 3))) + ((e)^(((sqrt(t)))))

#% cell typeset
zy = ((1)/(x)) + ((surd(x, 3))) + ((e)^(((sqrt(t)))))▮
--- clip
text "y = 1/x + surd(x, 3) + e^sqrt(t)"

=== Paste as math of text that does not read pastes the text
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Clip("f(") Ctrl+Shift+V
--- after
#% cell
f(▮

=== Down from the insertion point above enters a cell with boxes at its start
--- before
‖
#% cell typeset
y + ((e)^(((sqrt(t)))))
--- keys
Down "a"
--- boxes
a▮y + (e^√(t))

=== Up from the insertion point below enters its last line at the goal x (the line's start without one)
--- before
#% cell typeset
y + ((e)^(((sqrt(t)))))
‖
--- keys
Up "a"
--- boxes
a▮y + (e^√(t))
